From: Denys Vitali <denys@denv.it>
Subject: [PATCH] egl/dri2: treat an explicit DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID as no modifier

mutter passes EGL_DMA_BUF_PLANE0_MODIFIER_{LO,HI} = DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID for
implicit-modifier client buffers. With the pvr driver, the explicit-modifier
path (createImageFromDmaBufs2) fails with EGL_BAD_MATCH, so every EGL
Wayland client was killed with "failed to import supplied dmabufs". The same
buffer imports fine without modifier attributes (tested on the SGX540).
---
--- a/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c	2026-11-19 22:34:03.730668156 +0000
+++ b/src/egl/drivers/dri2/egl_dri2.c	2026-11-19 22:34:03.794667310 +0000
@@ -2876,6 +2876,12 @@
       has_modifier = true;
    }
 
+   /* An explicit DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID means "implicit modifier". mutter
+    * passes it for implicit-modifier client buffers, and the pvr driver
+    * rejects every explicit modifier (EGL_BAD_MATCH), so treat it as absent. */
+   if (has_modifier && modifier == DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID)
+      has_modifier = false;
+
    if (attrs.ProtectedContent) {
       if (dri2_dpy->image->base.version < 18 ||
           dri2_dpy->image->createImageFromDmaBufs3 == NULL) {
